{
  "_comment": [
    "`paint` is STORAGE ORDER and is APPEND-ONLY. A pixel is persisted as its index in this",
    "array (1-based; 0 is the eraser), so reordering or inserting anything before the end",
    "silently recolours every pixel already on the shared canvas. New colours go at the END.",
    "`displayOrder` is what the palette shows, and may be rearranged freely - it is a list of",
    "names, not indices. mg_pixelbattle_palette_test.js enforces both halves."
  ],
  "ocean": "#183443",
  "land": "#a5ab91",
  "paint": [
    { "name": "white",      "hex": "#ffffff" },
    { "name": "light_gray", "hex": "#c4c9cc" },
